# SABOTAGE: F7 slice gate sabotage — the ADR-025 flatten-conflict tripwire (build-integrity).
# `Samen.AbbrevRegistry.flatten_conflicts/1` no longer detects a 2-way lossy flattening
# (the real-world "first legitimate cross-host prefix reuse" case: the same abbrev owned by
# two namespaces with distinct owners). The `> 1` distinct-owner test is weakened to `> 2`,
# so a cross-host reuse (and a host-vs-global mismatch) go UNDETECTED, the compat shim's
# `load/0` silently picks one owner instead of failing closed, and the flattened-view
# verifier would false-positive on the shadowed resource. The samen_core tripwire red-paths
# MUST fail.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/abbrev_flatten_conflict_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RAISES fail-closed with a message naming ADR-025
# MUST_FAIL: reports the shadowed abbrev with its competing owners
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/abbrev_registry.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/abbrev_registry.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/abbrev_registry.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/abbrev_registry.ex
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ defmodule Samen.AbbrevRegistry do
     (host_sources ++ global_sources)
     |> Enum.group_by(fn {abbrev, _src_owner} -> abbrev end, fn {_abbrev, src_owner} -> src_owner end)
     |> Enum.filter(fn {_abbrev, src_owners} ->
-      src_owners |> Enum.map(fn {_src, owner} -> owner end) |> Enum.uniq() |> length() > 1
+      src_owners |> Enum.map(fn {_src, owner} -> owner end) |> Enum.uniq() |> length() > 2
     end)
     |> Enum.map(fn {abbrev, src_owners} -> %{abbrev: abbrev, owners: Enum.sort(src_owners)} end)
     |> Enum.sort_by(& &1.abbrev)
